From b2d0b62a9d96fc5639302ee8690dfa7a7ea3fa14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:24:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: the flips of a blocking commit share one wait
 of 3 s

nv_drm_atomic_commit() waits, after a blocking commit, for the flip event
of each CRTC of the commit in turn, up to 3 s for each (wait_event_timeout()
with 3 * HZ in the loop over the CRTCs). The flips of all of them went out
together, in nv_drm_atomic_apply_modeset_config(), so where their events do
not come the caller waits 3 s times the number of CRTCs. On the RTX 4080
SUPER, with three displays, Kodi's commit that turns off
the two outputs it does not use (and sets the mode of its own again) logged
"Flip event timeout on head 0", "head 1" and "head 2", 3.2 s apart, and its
interface stood still for 9.6 s; 1.0 did the same.

The wait has one end now, 3 s after the flips went out, for every CRTC of
the commit: each still gets its 3 s from the moment its flip went out, as
before, and the commit no longer adds them up. A CRTC whose turn comes after
that end is still waited for one tick, and its events are handled as on a
timeout before (the flip list is emptied and its events sent). The log line
keeps NVIDIA's words and says that the flips share the 3 s.

Why the events did not come is not known from the open code (the next patch
says how long each event of NVKMS kept the others waiting). Nothing changes
for a commit whose flip events come in time, nor for a non-blocking one.

Checked: the five modules build against Linux 7.3.5 with the compiler of
the image, with no new warning; the patch applies with --fuzz=0 after
9000 to 9079. Not run on a GPU: with three displays, the kernel log of a
start should have at most one "Flip event timeout" line for a commit, and
the interface of Kodi should not stand still for longer than 3 s.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c | 26 +++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
index 31a6f2c..248de04 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
@@ -921,6 +921,11 @@ int nv_drm_atomic_commit(struct drm_device *dev,
     struct drm_crtc *crtc = NULL;
     struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state = NULL;
     struct nv_drm_device *nv_dev = to_nv_device(dev);
+    /*
+     * Hades: the end of the wait for the flips of a blocking commit, one for
+     * all its CRTCs (set once they went out)
+     */
+    unsigned long hades_flip_deadline = 0;
 
     /*
      * XXX: drm_mode_config_funcs::atomic_commit() mandates to return -EBUSY
@@ -1006,6 +1011,16 @@ int nv_drm_atomic_commit(struct drm_device *dev,
         goto done;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Hades: the flips of every CRTC of the commit went out together, in
+     * nv_drm_atomic_apply_modeset_config(): each gets its 3 s from now. The
+     * wait below took 3 s for each CRTC in turn, so a commit whose flip events
+     * do not come (three outputs, one of them turned on and two turned off, on
+     * an RTX 4080 SUPER: "Flip event timeout on head 0",
+     * "head 1", "head 2", 3.2 s apart) held its caller for 9.6 s.
+     */
+    hades_flip_deadline = jiffies + 3 * HZ;
+
     for_each_old_crtc_in_state(state, crtc, crtc_state, i) {
         struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc = to_nv_crtc(crtc);
         struct nv_drm_crtc_state *nv_new_crtc_state =
@@ -1082,13 +1097,20 @@ int nv_drm_atomic_commit(struct drm_device *dev,
              * updating the list could not trick us into thinking the list is
              * empty when it isn't.
              */
+            /* Hades: what is left of the 3 s of the commit (at least a tick) */
+            long hades_left = (long)(hades_flip_deadline - jiffies);
+
+            if (hades_left < 1) {
+                hades_left = 1;
+            }
             if (wait_event_timeout(
                     nv_dev->flip_event_wq,
                     list_empty(&nv_crtc->flip_list),
-                    3 * HZ /* 3 second */) == 0) {
+                    hades_left) == 0) {
                 NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_ERR(
                     nv_dev,
-                    "Flip event timeout on head %u", nv_crtc->head);
+                    "Flip event timeout on head %u (Hades: the flips of a commit share 3 s)",
+                    nv_crtc->head);
                 while (!list_empty(&nv_crtc->flip_list)) {
                     __nv_drm_handle_flip_event(nv_crtc);
                 }
